The rule as written says the response-verdict check's answer ought to be unchanged between these two texts. The refusal heuristic decides the verdict only when no object can be recovered; whether a phrase occurred at all is a separate fact, refusal_phrase_in, recorded beside a recovered object (H36: a refusal followed by a form is a refusal and a form). Both texts contain a recoverable JSON object, so the verdict is JSON_OBJECT in both, and the presence or absence of 'I cannot' does not change it.